---
import SiteLayout from '../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import BookingLink from '../../components/BookingLink.astro';
import DiscoveryCall from '../../components/DiscoveryCall.astro';
---
<SiteLayout service="consulting" title="Consulting | TJ Maynes" description="I'm TJ Maynes. I build business automations, connect systems, and work with teams on AI workflows.">
  <main id="main">
    <section class="hero wrap" aria-labelledby="consulting-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">Consulting</p>
      <h1 id="consulting-title">I help businesses automate their work.</h1>
      <p class="lead">I work with you to understand a recurring task, figure out what can be automated, and build it. That might mean connecting apps, preparing a regular report, or writing a small internal tool.</p>
      <div class="actions"><BookingLink service="consulting" placement="hero" /><span class="call-note">Free 15-minute call</span></div>
    </section>

    <section class="section wrap split" aria-labelledby="work-title">
      <div><h2 id="work-title">What I work on</h2></div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>I build workflows that produce recurring reports, move information between systems, and handle incoming requests. I can also help you test where AI is useful for tasks such as drafting or extracting information.</p>
        <p>I use n8n for app integrations and workflows, and Codex, Claude, or Claude Code for scripts, internal tools, and other automation tasks. I’ll work with the tools you have and explain any additional software I recommend.</p>
        <p>If you have an engineering team, I can pair with your developers and help them understand and maintain what we build.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section wrap split" aria-labelledby="process-title">
      <div><h2 id="process-title">How I work</h2></div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>I’ll start by asking you to walk me through the process as it works today. I want to understand who uses it, which systems it touches, and what tends to go wrong.</p>
        <p>During the project, I’ll show you progress and ask for feedback. I test the workflow, including what happens when an input is missing or a service fails, and document how to run it.</p>
        <p>Before handing it over, I’ll walk you or your team through it. Your business should control the accounts and have access to the code and documentation.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section wrap split" aria-labelledby="pricing-title">
      <div><h2 id="pricing-title">Scope and fees</h2></div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>I quote implementation work at a fixed price once we’ve agreed on the scope. The quote covers the build, testing, documentation, and handoff.</p>
        <p>If I need to investigate before I can quote the build, I’ll suggest a smaller paid assessment and agree on its cost with you first.</p>
        <p>Software subscriptions, hosting, and AI usage are separate unless included in the quote. We’ll also agree on any maintenance or ongoing support before launch.</p>
        <p>If you’d prefer to learn to build the automation yourself, I also offer <a href="/services/coaching/">one-to-one coaching</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <DiscoveryCall service="consulting" />
  </main>
</SiteLayout>
